08:16.780 --> 08:18.840
Um, and you mentioned scaling in, too.

08:18.960 --> 08:22.140
Yeah, scaling in and scaling out is a really great thing to do.

08:22.640 --> 08:32.580
Um, scaling in allows you to potentially get a better entry or make it so maybe an inopportune entry that gets, like, you know, repainted on or something.

08:32.580 --> 08:39.060
And still has a chance of squeezing out some profits if, like, that position, you know, would have gotten stopped out or something.

08:39.060 --> 08:44.640
But you can just add a little more there because you started with, like, maybe a third of a percent instead of a full percent.

08:45.560 --> 08:53.700
And scaling out's great, too, man, because you take profit when, you know, when things get iffy, you secure profits and you're managing that risk.

08:53.800 --> 08:55.900
You're not thinking about the money you're taking off the table.

08:56.000 --> 08:59.920
